CREATED:20261006T152028Z
DESCRIPTION:Lessons from Latin America - Mini-Conference Series (2026-2027
 ) Workshop 1: Care Against Violence: Gender Violence\, Reproductive Justi
 ce\, and Social Reproduction\nDate: October 22-24\, 2026\nLocation: Duke 
 University | Hybrid\n\nSimultaneous interpretation (English-Spanish) avai
 lable for all sessions.\n\nWorkshop Day 2 of 2 - Saturday\, 10/24: \n\n10
 -12: Panel 4-Care in Practice \n\nLara Islinger (Leuphana University Lüne
 burg)\, "Transnational Feminist Organizing  - Abortion Accompaniment Acro
 ss Borders"\n\nHana Mesquita (Universidade Federal do Rio de Janeiro)\, "
 The Making of Feticide: A Reproductive Governance Analysis of Political a
 nd Biomedical Attacks on Legal Abortion in Brazil"\n\nLabila Sumayah Muso
 ke (Afya na Haki Institute and Initiative for Social and Economic Rights)
 \, "Sewn for his pleasure:  A decolonial and reproductive justice analysi
 s of the husband stitch"\n\nRespondent:  Tania Rispoli (Duke University)\
 n\n12-2: Lunch for all registered attendees\n\n2-4: Closing Round Table-C
 entral Themes and Future Research \n\nLucía Cavallero (Universidad de Bue
 nos Aires)\n\nElisabeth Jay Friedman (University of San Francisco)\n\nHol
 ly Worthen (Universidad Autónoma Benito Juárez-Oaxaca)\n\nFor the full wo
 rkshop schedule and registration\, see: https://revaluingcare.org/care-ag
 ainst-violence-gender-violence-reproductive-justice-and-social-reproducti
 on/\n\nCo-sponsors: History\, Trinity College\, Gender\, Sexuality\, and 
 Feminist Studies\, Franklin Humanities Institute\, Center for Latin Ameri
 can and Caribbean Studies (CLACS)\, National Endowment for the Humanities
 \, and the Vice President for Research & Innovation
