CREATED:20260913T204541Z
DESCRIPTION:Spend an afternoon exploring space through art\, science\, pho
 tography\, and hands-on activities.\n\nJoin us for a free\, family-friend
 ly event celebrating Cassandra Klos's exhibition "Cosmic Origins" at CDS.
  Explore the exhibition and imagine what life beyond Earth might look lik
 e through activities and demonstrations presented by the Museum of Life a
 nd Science\, Stargazing Devils\, Click! Photography Festival\, Duke's SPA
 CE Initiative\, and more.\n\nActivities will include asteroid mining\, su
 n gazing\, a camera obscura experience\, and a special exhibition-related
  activity with Cassandra Klos. We'll also have slushies and popcorn!\n\nW
 ith Halloween just around the corner\, visitors of all ages are encourage
 d to come dressed for space exploration. Whether you're an astronaut\, al
 ien\, scientist\, rover\, or explorer\, we'd love to see your cosmic crea
 tivity.\n\nFree and open to all ages!\n\nOrganized by CDS in collaboratio
 n with the Duke SPACE Initiative\, the Museum of Life and Science\, and C
 lick! Photography Festival. More info about the exhibition: https://docum
 entarystudies.duke.edu/upcoming-exhibitions.\n\n*Directions and Parking*\
 n\nFind directions and bus information here:https://documentarystudies.du
 ke.edu/directions.\n\nFree parking will be available in the parking lots 
 behind the CDS buildings\, and on W. Pettigrew St. between Swift Avenue a
 nd the Freedom Bridge. Please park in the direction of traffic.
DURATION:PT4H
