CONTACT;X-BEDEWORK-UID=00f1fcdb-0f068baf-010f-068baf83-00000004:None
CREATED:20260416T173519Z
DESCRIPTION:Before a preacher reaches the sermon's first sentence\, a cong
 regation is already learning whom to trust. A Geneva gown. A rhinestoned 
 stole. A preacher's voice breaking into song. Each can teach a room what 
 authority is supposed to look and sound like-and who seems strangely out 
 of place. Drawing on his recently published article in the Journal of the
  American Academy of Religion\, Brett McKinley Pardue brings Christian ve
 sture into conversation with drag performance and the visual and sonic li
 fe of worship. What does preaching communicate before words-and what if f
 aithful authority arrives dressed differently than we expect?\n\nThe Cong
 regation's weekly Adult Forum offers a variety of guest speakers\, presen
 tations and discussions on a wide range of thought-provoking topics\, inc
 luding Biblical studies\, current social issues and the work of mission a
 gencies.  Adult Forum aims to deepen the faith and understanding of adult
 s through shared learning experiences. Classes include programs and discu
 ssions on contemporary issues in light of Christian teachings.
DURATION:PT1H
DTSTAMP:20260928T181951Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261025T094500
LAST-MODIFIED:20260928T181951Z
