CREATED:20260915T181402Z
DESCRIPTION:Organist Joshua Stafford plays live musical accompaniment for 
 this screening of the 1922 silent film "Nosferatu."\n\nView the program f
 or this event here: https://chapel.duke.edu/nosferatu-symphony-horror-192
 2 .\n\n*** This event is sold out. Beginning at 6:00 p.m. on the day of t
 he event\, a standby line will be available outside of the main entrance 
 of the Duke Chapel. If seats become available prior to the start of the e
 vent\, tickets will be distributed to those in the standby line on a firs
 t-come\, first-served basis. Guests must remain in line to retain their p
 lace\, and tickets will be limited to one per person. ***\n\nA livestream
  of the film with musical accompaniment is available here: https://www.yo
 utube.com/live/81_qysErCVg .\n\nAcclaimed for his "innate yet highly matu
 re musicality\," Stafford was named First Prize Winner in the Longwood Ga
 rdens International Organ Competition in 2016. Mr. Stafford regularly per
 forms on the world's two largest pipe organs at the former Wanamaker stor
 e in Philadelphia and Atlantic City's Boardwalk Hall. At Duke\, Stafford 
 will perform on the Chapel's Aeolian organ.\n\nThe screening and performa
 nce is part of the Organ Recital Series.
DURATION:PT1H
DTSTAMP:20261023T170526Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261025T190000
LAST-MODIFIED:20261023T170526Z
