CREATED:20260226T141817Z
DESCRIPTION:An "Independent Thinkers" Conversation with Katherine Mangu-Wa
 rd hosted by Frank Bruni\, Duke professor and New York Times columnist\nO
 ct. 26\, 6 p.m.\, Penn Pavilion\n\nFew people's ideologies are wholly and
  neatly represented by the Democratic or Republican party. But what else 
 is there? What's the meaning of a different label? And is wearing one a r
 oute out of the country's ruinous partisanship?\n\nPlease join Frank Brun
 i for a spirited conversation - part of his "Independent Thinkers" series
  of events - with Katherine Mangu-Ward\, the editor in chief of Reason ma
 gazine\, which is the country's leading libertarian journal.\n\nMangu-War
 d not only holds the top job at Reason\, the magazine of "free minds and 
 free markets\," but also has written many of its cover stories\, includin
 g one that defended plastic bags and another that made a case for not vot
 ing\, and appears on its weekly podcast. She has contributed to The New Y
 ork Times\, The Wall Street Journal and The Washington Post\; did a TED T
 alk about what capitalism gets right (and government gets wrong)\; and ha
 s been spotlighted on many television shows\, including HBO's Real Time w
 ith Bill Maher. \n\nFrank Bruni teaches at Duke's Sanford School of Publi
 c Policy as part of the DeWitt Wallace Center for Media and Democracy. He
 's also a longtime writer for The New York Times and the author of five b
 estselling books.\n\nFrank's "Independent Thinkers" conversations with pu
 blic figures who defy reductive political labels are part of the Provost'
 s Initiative on Pluralism\, Free Inquiry and Belonging.
DURATION:PT1H30M
DTSTAMP:20261002T150001Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261026T180000
LAST-MODIFIED:20261002T150001Z
